1
00:01:03,065 --> 00:01:06,670
Ma'am, can you please put up your seat?

2
00:01:07,337 --> 00:01:09,037
Thank you.

3
00:01:43,704 --> 00:01:46,737
[Welcome to Korea, Mantua]

4
00:02:05,870 --> 00:02:09,293
[Arrivals]

5
00:02:09,293 --> 00:02:11,137
Mr. Gong Eun Tae?

6
00:02:12,185 --> 00:02:13,665
Hello.

7
00:02:13,665 --> 00:02:17,204
I'm Martina, Head of Merchandising at Mantua.

8
00:02:18,121 --> 00:02:22,437
Oh, hello. I'm Gong Eun Tae
from Hongsung Sales.

9
00:02:23,525 --> 00:02:27,289
Surprised to hear me speak Korean?

10
00:02:27,289 --> 00:02:30,865
Yes. I assumed you'd be Italian, of course.

11
00:02:30,865 --> 00:02:32,653
I am Italian.

12
00:02:32,653 --> 00:02:34,237
It's been a while since I was in Korea.

13
00:02:34,237 --> 00:02:35,397
Oh...

14
00:02:35,397 --> 00:02:37,504
Why did you come all the way to the airport?

15
00:02:37,504 --> 00:02:39,433
We could've met at the office.

16
00:02:39,433 --> 00:02:42,204
- Of course, I had to...
- When you're overly welcoming,

17
00:02:42,204 --> 00:02:44,370
people can read your intentions, huh?

18
00:02:44,370 --> 00:02:47,204
How hard is what you're about to ask?

19
00:02:48,270 --> 00:02:49,841
Let's go.

20
00:02:49,841 --> 00:02:53,057
I can't wait to find out why you had me fly

21
00:02:53,057 --> 00:02:55,370
all the way to Korea.

22
00:03:03,004 --> 00:03:05,170
[The Ordinary Jackpot, Subtitle]

23
00:03:05,170 --> 00:03:11,117
[Episode 9, Interpreting the Past]

24
00:03:11,117 --> 00:03:13,441
Mr. Yang, about Mantua,

25
00:03:13,441 --> 00:03:16,870
their ownership structure is complicated,
and they're all privately owned.

26
00:03:16,870 --> 00:03:19,404
There's no way they don't have
any accounting records.

27
00:03:19,404 --> 00:03:22,305
What about that Martina?
Did you look into her background?

28
00:03:22,305 --> 00:03:24,537
Well, about that...

29
00:03:26,025 --> 00:03:28,070
there's no data on her at all.

30
00:03:28,070 --> 00:03:29,070
How can there be nothing?

31
00:03:29,070 --> 00:03:31,037
Has she only worked at Mantua her whole life?

32
00:03:31,037 --> 00:03:32,604
It seems so.

33
00:03:32,604 --> 00:03:35,837
Darn it, who is this woman?

34
00:03:44,297 --> 00:03:46,570
Here's everything you ordered.

35
00:03:47,301 --> 00:03:49,404
- Thank you, sir.
- Enjoy.

36
00:03:56,629 --> 00:03:59,537
[Risk & Mitigation Plan]

37
00:04:05,809 --> 00:04:08,837
The Chinese market...

38
00:04:08,837 --> 00:04:11,553
What do you think?

39
00:04:11,553 --> 00:04:13,813
Well...

40
00:04:13,813 --> 00:04:16,017
It's not bad, but...

41
00:04:16,017 --> 00:04:19,770
I doubt you made this move
just for margins like these.

42
00:04:21,370 --> 00:04:24,404
CGM has entered the Korean market.

43
00:04:25,413 --> 00:04:27,961
You should've led with that.

44
00:04:27,961 --> 00:04:32,070
Wasn't CGM already in Korea as a vendor?

45
00:04:32,070 --> 00:04:36,904
They're setting up a Korean branch
to control their brands directly.

46
00:04:36,904 --> 00:04:40,637
Of course, Korea isn't their only target.

47
00:04:40,637 --> 00:04:42,709
They want to use Korea as a logistics hub

48
00:04:42,709 --> 00:04:45,925
and enter China while avoiding tariffs.

49
00:04:45,925 --> 00:04:50,633
So Hongsung wants to enter
China first with Mantua's backing?

50
00:04:50,633 --> 00:04:53,404
If Mantua enters China first,

51
00:04:53,404 --> 00:04:54,984
CGM won't be able to use its capital

52
00:04:54,984 --> 00:04:58,304
to pressure the Korean market as it does now.

53
00:05:12,365 --> 00:05:14,665
Is there coffee at the office?

54
00:05:14,665 --> 00:05:17,893
Well, we have a machine,

55
00:05:17,893 --> 00:05:19,770
but the temperature isn't quite right,

56
00:05:19,770 --> 00:05:22,670
so I brought this from a café I often go to.

57
00:05:23,429 --> 00:05:24,817
You know what?

58
00:05:24,817 --> 00:05:28,004
The soul of the person
making it goes into the coffee.

59
00:05:34,870 --> 00:05:36,857
This person isn't a mere merchant.

60
00:05:36,857 --> 00:05:40,837
This coffee wasn't made for someone else.

61
00:05:47,125 --> 00:05:49,133
Mr. Gong,

62
00:05:49,133 --> 00:05:50,970
I don't want to fight CGM.

63
00:05:50,970 --> 00:05:54,377
They're not exactly clean players.

64
00:05:54,377 --> 00:05:59,604
Then you don't mind
if CGM takes over the Chinese market?

65
00:06:00,305 --> 00:06:01,917
In the Bible,

66
00:06:01,917 --> 00:06:06,470
there's a parable about workers
hired in the morning and evening.

67
00:06:06,470 --> 00:06:08,204
Have you heard of it?

68
00:06:08,204 --> 00:06:09,465
Oh, yes.

69
00:06:09,465 --> 00:06:13,970
The one where the owner pays
two workers the same wage?

70
00:06:13,970 --> 00:06:15,870
Naturally, they'd complain.

71
00:06:15,870 --> 00:06:19,070
They worked different hours
but got paid the same.

72
00:06:19,070 --> 00:06:22,905
When the morning workers complained,
the owner said,

73
00:06:22,905 --> 00:06:27,461
"I gave you what I promised.
Why are you complaining?"

74
00:06:27,461 --> 00:06:30,533
We're already doing the work we're given

75
00:06:30,533 --> 00:06:33,273
and getting what we're owed.

76
00:06:33,273 --> 00:06:36,670
Wherever CGM expands
and however much they make

77
00:06:36,670 --> 00:06:39,405
has nothing to do with us.

78
00:06:39,405 --> 00:06:42,337
Then would you be fine

79
00:06:42,337 --> 00:06:46,770
if the evening workers took all the wages
earned by the morning workers?

80
00:06:46,770 --> 00:06:51,037
More than 60 or 70%
of Mantua's buyers are probably

81
00:06:51,037 --> 00:06:53,770
from Korea, China, Japan, and East Asia.

82
00:06:53,770 --> 00:06:56,525
And China likely makes up the largest share.

83
00:06:56,525 --> 00:06:59,829
If CGM sets up a warehouse in China,

84
00:06:59,829 --> 00:07:04,865
why would buyers in and around Guangzhou
bother doing business with Mantua?

85
00:07:04,865 --> 00:07:06,669
If CGM enters China,

86
00:07:06,669 --> 00:07:11,904
Mantua won't just lose China,
but the entire East Asian market.

87
00:07:13,204 --> 00:07:17,809
How much of our business
do you think comes from retailers?

88
00:07:17,809 --> 00:07:20,997
That's not enough to justify
going to war with CGM.

89
00:07:20,997 --> 00:07:23,570
The war has already begun.

90
00:07:23,570 --> 00:07:27,704
All we're asking is
for Mantua to join the fight.

91
00:07:29,593 --> 00:07:32,669
I think I need some time to think.

92
00:07:32,669 --> 00:07:34,970
Of course. Take all the time you need.

93
00:07:34,970 --> 00:07:38,770
But could you give me a rough timeline?

94
00:07:38,770 --> 00:07:41,777
It won't take long.
I'll decide while I'm in Korea.

95
00:07:41,777 --> 00:07:46,329
But I'd like someone
to show me around while I'm here.

96
00:07:46,329 --> 00:07:49,425
It's been a while,
so I'd like to look around.

97
00:07:49,425 --> 00:07:51,105
I'll show you around.

98
00:07:51,105 --> 00:07:53,849
No, assign your junior staff.

99
00:07:53,849 --> 00:07:55,704
If we end up working together,

100
00:07:55,704 --> 00:07:58,865
we'll be working mostly
with Hongsung's junior staff, won't we?

101
00:07:58,865 --> 00:08:01,025
This is a long-term business.

102
00:08:01,025 --> 00:08:04,570
You two could get promoted
into management and move on.

103
00:08:13,293 --> 00:08:16,049
Ji Hye, you'll have to
handle the VIP reception.

104
00:08:16,049 --> 00:08:18,177
What? Me?

105
00:08:18,177 --> 00:08:21,741
I'll explain later.
Just request a company car first.

106
00:08:21,741 --> 00:08:23,537
Oh, okay.

107
00:08:25,485 --> 00:08:26,637
Mr. Gong isn't going?

108
00:08:26,637 --> 00:08:27,837
Ugh, I don't know.

109
00:08:27,837 --> 00:08:29,893
That Martina woman is impossible to talk to.

110
00:08:29,893 --> 00:08:31,837
I can't tell what she's thinking.

111
00:08:42,170 --> 00:08:44,561
[Jung Sun Hyuk, Head of CGM Korea]

112
00:08:44,561 --> 00:08:46,261
Come in.

113
00:08:47,293 --> 00:08:48,993
Mr. Jung.

114
00:08:56,037 --> 00:08:58,304
[Team Leader Jung Sun Hyuk, Hongsung]

115
00:09:11,769 --> 00:09:13,237
Oh, dear.

116
00:09:13,237 --> 00:09:14,970
[Kim Soon Wook, Executive Director,
Belmore Department Store]

117
00:09:15,833 --> 00:09:18,861
- Yes, Mr. Kim.
<i>- Sorry, I missed your call earlier.</i>

118
00:09:18,861 --> 00:09:20,141
No problem at all.

119
00:09:20,141 --> 00:09:22,004
You called about the stores, right?

120
00:09:22,004 --> 00:09:25,953
Yes. I don't understand
why the commission suddenly went up.

121
00:09:25,953 --> 00:09:28,270
<i>I know. I just heard about it myself.</i>

122
00:09:28,270 --> 00:09:30,549
<i>It seems upper management
decided to go that way.</i>

123
00:09:30,549 --> 00:09:34,353
Mr. Kim, Hongsung pulled out
instead of taking 20%, didn't they?

124
00:09:34,353 --> 00:09:36,337
Then you should keep it at 20% for us.

125
00:09:36,337 --> 00:09:39,557
With Hongsung out, we can't accept 22%.

126
00:09:39,557 --> 00:09:41,170
Oh, is that so?

127
00:09:41,170 --> 00:09:45,805
We agreed to go up to 22 if Hongsung took 20.

128
00:09:45,805 --> 00:09:48,661
<i>Exactly. If Hongsung had taken it.</i>

129
00:09:48,661 --> 00:09:51,109
Just consider it as they did.

130
00:09:51,109 --> 00:09:52,737
But, sir...

131
00:09:52,737 --> 00:09:55,333
No, wait... that's...

132
00:09:55,333 --> 00:09:56,929
<i>- Mr. Jung.</i>
- Yes.

133
00:09:56,929 --> 00:10:00,181
<i>Don't take this personally. Think about it.</i>

134
00:10:00,181 --> 00:10:06,237
We gave up a stable partner like Hongsung
to work with you, didn't we?

135
00:10:06,237 --> 00:10:07,670
This business may seem

136
00:10:07,670 --> 00:10:11,237
<i>complicated, but it's pretty simple.</i>

137
00:10:11,237 --> 00:10:13,337
<i>We make the call because we think it'll work,</i>

138
00:10:13,337 --> 00:10:14,877
<i>and if you don't think it will,</i>

139
00:10:14,877 --> 00:10:17,237
you can walk away.

140
00:10:17,237 --> 00:10:18,949
If you're walking away, say so now.

141
00:10:18,949 --> 00:10:21,070
<i>Don't change your story later.</i>

142
00:10:23,004 --> 00:10:25,817
Alright. We'll go with 22%.

143
00:10:25,817 --> 00:10:29,425
But I'd appreciate it if you could
freeze the regular line.

144
00:10:29,425 --> 00:10:31,870
<i>No, we can't.</i>

145
00:10:31,870 --> 00:10:33,770
Keep it the same.

146
00:10:41,285 --> 00:10:44,149
Understood. Let's do that.

147
00:10:44,149 --> 00:10:46,570
<i>Alright, bye.</i>

148
00:10:54,521 --> 00:10:57,970
Darn it! Seriously!

149
00:11:03,265 --> 00:11:04,437
Team Leader Joo.

150
00:11:04,437 --> 00:11:05,437
Yes, sir.

151
00:11:05,437 --> 00:11:09,093
I need to find out what Hongsung is up to.

152
00:11:09,093 --> 00:11:12,337
Do you think Hongsung has another strategy?

153
00:11:12,337 --> 00:11:13,759
I think they're just

154
00:11:13,759 --> 00:11:17,437
planning to survive on the money
they make from the penalties.

155
00:11:17,437 --> 00:11:18,701
No,

156
00:11:18,701 --> 00:11:20,885
Hongsung won't back down this easily.

157
00:11:20,885 --> 00:11:22,785
They've definitely got something.

158
00:11:22,785 --> 00:11:26,185
If we let Hongsung get the better of us now,

159
00:11:26,185 --> 00:11:27,529
we might as well shut everything down.

160
00:11:27,529 --> 00:11:29,337
You know what I mean?

161
00:11:29,337 --> 00:11:33,537
Find out exactly
what Hongsung is thinking. Got it?

162
00:11:34,173 --> 00:11:36,804
Yes, sir.

163
00:11:56,370 --> 00:11:59,025
Hello, ma'am. I'm Lee Ji Hye.

164
00:11:59,025 --> 00:12:01,485
She'll be showing you around
while you're in Korea.

165
00:12:01,485 --> 00:12:03,870
Her Italian is excellent too.

166
00:12:18,609 --> 00:12:20,309
Let's go.

167
00:12:31,370 --> 00:12:33,270
Call me right away if there's any problem.

168
00:12:33,270 --> 00:12:34,721
I'll be standing by.

169
00:12:34,721 --> 00:12:36,604
Yes, Mr. Gong.

170
00:12:56,737 --> 00:12:58,804
[Sungnyemun Gate]

171
00:13:05,570 --> 00:13:08,925
There's somewhere
I'd like to stop by. Is that okay?

172
00:13:08,925 --> 00:13:11,589
Sure. Where would you like to go?

173
00:13:11,589 --> 00:13:15,204
I'm curious where you bought
the clothes you're wearing.

174
00:13:15,921 --> 00:13:18,004
My outfit?

175
00:13:22,570 --> 00:13:25,404
[Hongin Intersection]

176
00:13:42,465 --> 00:13:44,445
There's no price tag?

177
00:13:44,445 --> 00:13:46,793
Excuse me, how much is this?

178
00:13:46,793 --> 00:13:49,641
Just give me 50,000 won.

179
00:13:49,641 --> 00:13:52,304
Don't tell anyone else.

180
00:13:52,304 --> 00:13:55,070
50,000 won... that's 30 euros.

181
00:13:55,733 --> 00:13:58,993
You bought those clothes here?

182
00:13:58,993 --> 00:14:01,370
Yes. They have all kinds of clothes here.

183
00:14:01,370 --> 00:14:05,204
Whenever fashion shows opened
in Milan, Paris, London, or New York,

184
00:14:05,204 --> 00:14:08,004
identical pieces would appear
here the next day.

185
00:14:08,004 --> 00:14:11,481
If they didn't sell in three days,
they'd be thrown out.

186
00:14:11,481 --> 00:14:13,493
It's fallen off quite a bit since then,

187
00:14:13,493 --> 00:14:18,157
but it's still one of the best places
in the world for the latest trends.

188
00:14:18,157 --> 00:14:20,904
If that were still true,
it wouldn't have declined.

189
00:14:25,073 --> 00:14:29,537
Is there another reason
you shop here besides the price?

190
00:14:30,725 --> 00:14:34,470
This is where I fell in love with clothes.

191
00:14:34,470 --> 00:14:39,604
Maybe this is also what made me
want to work for Hongsung.

192
00:14:39,604 --> 00:14:42,970
You know that the same design
doesn't mean the same clothes, right?

193
00:14:42,970 --> 00:14:46,437
Details are everything in clothing.

194
00:14:47,604 --> 00:14:50,029
There are plenty of good clothes here too.

195
00:14:50,029 --> 00:14:54,104
Even big brands often buy items
from here just the way they are.

196
00:14:58,169 --> 00:15:01,604
So that's what you chose?

197
00:15:03,417 --> 00:15:06,204
You don't like my clothes?

198
00:15:07,501 --> 00:15:09,804
It's a 2022 summer Varnessa dress

199
00:15:09,804 --> 00:15:13,553
blended with a 2023 Marezi skirt design.

200
00:15:13,553 --> 00:15:17,237
The fabric is a Chinese
cotton-polyester blend.

201
00:15:17,237 --> 00:15:21,237
It's been cut carelessly, without considering
how the seams would line up.

202
00:15:21,237 --> 00:15:23,170
But let's put that aside.

203
00:15:23,804 --> 00:15:29,070
Do you even know
how to care for different fabrics?

204
00:15:31,570 --> 00:15:34,004
Doctors aren't always healthy.

205
00:15:34,004 --> 00:15:36,237
People who sell alcohol
don't need to be drinkers.

206
00:15:36,237 --> 00:15:38,670
But clothes are different.

207
00:15:38,670 --> 00:15:41,137
If you sell clothes,

208
00:15:41,137 --> 00:15:43,370
you should know clothes.

209
00:16:00,784 --> 00:16:03,017
- Mr. Gong.
- Yes?

210
00:16:03,017 --> 00:16:05,517
Can I ask you something?

211
00:16:05,517 --> 00:16:07,849
You're going to ask anyway, right?

212
00:16:07,849 --> 00:16:10,081
Why did you send Ji Hye?

213
00:16:10,081 --> 00:16:11,825
Because she's the youngest.

214
00:16:11,825 --> 00:16:14,349
Martina specifically
asked for a junior team member.

215
00:16:14,349 --> 00:16:16,537
You could've just made an excuse
and sent Gi Tae.

216
00:16:16,537 --> 00:16:20,069
Martina doesn't know everyone on our team.

217
00:16:20,069 --> 00:16:23,049
And I thought Ji Hye would do a good job.

218
00:16:23,049 --> 00:16:26,870
How can someone like you
be worrying this much?

219
00:16:28,337 --> 00:16:32,177
I'd be worried about anyone going,
not just Ji Hye.

220
00:16:32,177 --> 00:16:33,417
Exactly.

221
00:16:33,417 --> 00:16:36,470
I'm worried
that I can't focus on work either.

222
00:16:51,689 --> 00:16:52,809
- Mr. Yang.
- Yeah?

223
00:16:52,809 --> 00:16:54,004
Looking for something?

224
00:16:54,004 --> 00:16:57,504
Well, I have a coffee I drink,
but I can't find it.

225
00:17:02,470 --> 00:17:04,705
Don't bother. I'll do it.

226
00:17:04,705 --> 00:17:06,933
I'm already at it. Just sit tight.

227
00:17:06,933 --> 00:17:09,749
Just go easy on the water.

228
00:17:09,749 --> 00:17:12,470
Sure. I'll make it just right.

229
00:17:14,470 --> 00:17:16,337
You're pretty busy these days, huh?

230
00:17:16,337 --> 00:17:18,745
Don't even ask. I'm dying over here.

231
00:17:18,745 --> 00:17:20,749
Looks like it.

232
00:17:20,749 --> 00:17:23,677
Have you heard from CGM?

233
00:17:23,677 --> 00:17:24,677
Sorry?

234
00:17:24,677 --> 00:17:26,505
No, I guess they don't need me.

235
00:17:26,505 --> 00:17:28,904
What?

236
00:17:28,904 --> 00:17:31,270
Were you going to leave if they did?

237
00:17:31,270 --> 00:17:33,313
Well, I would've thought about it.

238
00:17:33,313 --> 00:17:35,361
It's not something
you can solve by staying loyal.

239
00:17:35,361 --> 00:17:40,277
Honestly, if CGM takes over Korea,
we'd all be out of work.

240
00:17:40,277 --> 00:17:43,297
We're not going down that easily.
Don't worry.

241
00:17:43,297 --> 00:17:45,821
Why? Do we have something up our sleeve?

242
00:17:45,821 --> 00:17:47,289
Of course.

243
00:17:47,289 --> 00:17:50,613
So just sit tight and wait.

244
00:17:50,613 --> 00:17:54,293
Oh, I saw Team 5 booked
a meeting room this morning.

245
00:17:54,293 --> 00:17:56,697
Is that related to this?

246
00:17:56,697 --> 00:17:58,404
Don't ask too many questions.

247
00:17:58,404 --> 00:18:02,553
Come on, I swear I'll keep it
to myself, please.

248
00:18:02,553 --> 00:18:05,337
I'm just really anxious.

249
00:18:25,697 --> 00:18:28,101
Would you like an explanation of the menu?

250
00:18:28,101 --> 00:18:31,089
No. Please order for me.

251
00:18:31,089 --> 00:18:32,725
We'll take a look and then order.

252
00:18:32,725 --> 00:18:34,425
Okay.

253
00:18:36,837 --> 00:18:40,157
[Appetizer]

254
00:18:40,157 --> 00:18:43,417
Is there anything specific you'd like to eat?

255
00:18:43,417 --> 00:18:45,433
Don't ask me.

256
00:18:45,433 --> 00:18:47,529
Order whatever you want.

257
00:18:47,529 --> 00:18:49,970
Oh, okay.

258
00:18:54,069 --> 00:18:57,033
This is Batasiolo Barolo, 2020 vintage.

259
00:18:57,033 --> 00:18:59,041
Is this the wine you ordered?

260
00:18:59,041 --> 00:19:00,741
Yes.

261
00:19:12,345 --> 00:19:14,037
Would you like to taste it?

262
00:19:14,037 --> 00:19:15,770
I'll do it.

263
00:19:38,893 --> 00:19:40,593
It's good.

264
00:19:41,445 --> 00:19:43,170
Thank you.

265
00:19:59,305 --> 00:20:01,204
As for the wine,

266
00:20:01,204 --> 00:20:03,453
who recommended it?

267
00:20:03,453 --> 00:20:09,005
Oh, I chose one I thought would pair well,
from wines I've tried before.

268
00:20:09,005 --> 00:20:10,817
You've had it before?

269
00:20:10,817 --> 00:20:12,517
Yes, ma'am.

270
00:20:41,321 --> 00:20:43,397
I heard you speak some Italian?

271
00:20:43,397 --> 00:20:45,970
Yes. I'm still learning.

272
00:20:48,837 --> 00:20:53,737
Is there a particular reason
you chose this place?

273
00:20:54,409 --> 00:20:57,069
They have an excellent wine list.

274
00:20:57,069 --> 00:21:00,421
I thought any good meal
should be paired with wine.

275
00:21:00,421 --> 00:21:01,737
And if we're having wine,

276
00:21:01,737 --> 00:21:05,993
I thought we should come somewhere
with a good selection of Italian wines.

277
00:21:05,993 --> 00:21:07,561
And?

278
00:21:07,561 --> 00:21:10,633
I wanted something we couldn't have in Italy.

279
00:21:10,633 --> 00:21:13,925
Since you've been away
from Korea for so long,

280
00:21:13,925 --> 00:21:16,893
I thought modern Korean cuisine
would be better than traditional Korean food.

281
00:21:16,893 --> 00:21:18,581
That's why I chose this place.

282
00:21:18,581 --> 00:21:23,070
They serve Korean food
that pairs well with good wine.

283
00:21:24,125 --> 00:21:25,317
Good.

284
00:21:25,317 --> 00:21:27,729
I'm glad you like it.

285
00:21:27,729 --> 00:21:33,225
Food reveals as much about a person

286
00:21:33,225 --> 00:21:37,385
as their clothes do.

287
00:21:37,385 --> 00:21:40,145
Have you figured out
what kind of person I am?

288
00:21:40,145 --> 00:21:42,137
Either someone who's good at lying,

289
00:21:42,137 --> 00:21:44,937
or someone consumed by vanity.

290
00:21:46,281 --> 00:21:47,369
Excuse me?

291
00:21:47,369 --> 00:21:50,297
Your salary can't be much,

292
00:21:50,297 --> 00:21:53,749
and a woman who buys 30-euro clothes

293
00:21:53,749 --> 00:21:58,005
but has tasted wine like this

294
00:21:58,005 --> 00:22:02,817
has to be one of two things.

295
00:22:02,817 --> 00:22:05,693
Either you've never tasted it,

296
00:22:05,693 --> 00:22:09,285
or you're living way beyond your means.

297
00:22:09,285 --> 00:22:11,104
What do you think?

298
00:22:13,253 --> 00:22:16,904
Neither makes you very trustworthy.

299
00:22:23,704 --> 00:22:26,104
[Lee Ji Hye, Associate, Team 5]

300
00:22:30,245 --> 00:22:31,457
Yes, Ji Hye.

301
00:22:31,457 --> 00:22:33,701
Mr. Gong.

302
00:22:33,701 --> 00:22:35,153
<i>How is it going?</i>

303
00:22:35,153 --> 00:22:37,104
Mar...

304
00:22:38,733 --> 00:22:40,893
I think Martina is out of her mind.

305
00:22:40,893 --> 00:22:42,577
<i>Is it that bad?</i>

306
00:22:42,577 --> 00:22:46,337
I think she's determined
to nitpick every single thing.

307
00:22:48,033 --> 00:22:50,970
<i>How far do I have to accommodate her?</i>

308
00:22:50,970 --> 00:22:52,505
<i>Ji Hye,</i>

309
00:22:52,505 --> 00:22:55,237
you know we desperately need Mantua, right?

310
00:22:55,237 --> 00:22:56,445
Yes, of course.

311
00:22:56,445 --> 00:22:58,333
<i>Even so,</i>

312
00:22:58,333 --> 00:23:00,465
you don't have to give her
everything she wants.

313
00:23:00,465 --> 00:23:04,833
If we can't have Mantua,
we'll find another way.

314
00:23:04,833 --> 00:23:09,817
We can't do business with someone
who has us by the throat.

315
00:23:09,817 --> 00:23:12,404
<i>Even if things aren't fair,
you have to pretend they are.</i>

316
00:23:12,404 --> 00:23:14,973
<i>You have to at least
pretend to consider each other.</i>

317
00:23:14,973 --> 00:23:18,870
Without that much hypocrisy,
you can't work together.

318
00:23:19,901 --> 00:23:21,977
Then...

319
00:23:21,977 --> 00:23:25,793
If she makes unreasonable demands,
you don't have to accept them.

320
00:23:25,793 --> 00:23:28,005
Alright, Mr. Gong. I'll do that.

321
00:23:28,005 --> 00:23:29,421
I'll call you back later.

322
00:23:29,421 --> 00:23:31,121
<i>Alright.</i>

323
00:23:41,841 --> 00:23:43,770
She'll be okay, right?

324
00:24:03,877 --> 00:24:07,153
Do you need anything else
when you check into the hotel?

325
00:24:07,153 --> 00:24:08,985
Why are you asking me?

326
00:24:08,985 --> 00:24:11,537
The person preparing it should know.

327
00:24:15,353 --> 00:24:17,870
I've prepared some cheese
and prosciutto to go with the wine,

328
00:24:17,870 --> 00:24:20,770
along with brown melon,
and had them placed in your room.

329
00:24:20,770 --> 00:24:23,617
I've also made sure
there's plenty of water and towels.

330
00:24:23,617 --> 00:24:26,305
I've compiled a list of places to visit
and restaurants for tomorrow

331
00:24:26,305 --> 00:24:28,661
and left it in a folder on the table.

332
00:24:28,661 --> 00:24:32,749
I was just asking if there was
anything else you needed.

333
00:24:32,749 --> 00:24:35,537
Do you think that's enough?

334
00:24:37,589 --> 00:24:41,437
If you tell me what else you need,
I'll prepare it.

335
00:24:42,041 --> 00:24:44,781
The current size of the Chinese market,

336
00:24:44,781 --> 00:24:47,870
the benefits we'd gain by entering China,

337
00:24:47,870 --> 00:24:51,389
and the losses we'd suffer
if CGM enters China.

338
00:24:51,389 --> 00:24:53,970
What I need isn't wine or towels

339
00:24:53,970 --> 00:24:57,337
but data like that, wouldn't you say?

340
00:25:23,917 --> 00:25:25,617
Ma'am,

341
00:25:26,457 --> 00:25:30,209
I'll contact the office
and prepare that data immediately.

342
00:25:30,209 --> 00:25:32,073
You should've prepared it beforehand.

343
00:25:32,073 --> 00:25:35,601
It was prepared. I just failed to bring it.

344
00:25:35,601 --> 00:25:38,137
That's exactly the problem.

345
00:25:38,137 --> 00:25:41,601
Did you think catering to my whims
would be enough?

346
00:25:41,601 --> 00:25:44,337
Is this how Hongsung does business?

347
00:25:45,673 --> 00:25:47,637
Tomorrow,

348
00:25:47,637 --> 00:25:50,004
have them send someone else.

349
00:26:03,204 --> 00:26:05,437
[Lee Ji Hye, Associate, Team 5]

350
00:26:09,421 --> 00:26:10,649
Yes, Ji Hye.

351
00:26:10,649 --> 00:26:12,349
Mr. Gong.

352
00:26:14,401 --> 00:26:16,270
I'm sorry.

353
00:26:17,021 --> 00:26:18,409
What happened?

354
00:26:18,409 --> 00:26:21,429
<i>She went back to the hotel upset.</i>

355
00:26:21,429 --> 00:26:24,204
<i>She told us to send someone else tomorrow.</i>

356
00:26:24,204 --> 00:26:28,905
I did my best,
but I just wasn't ready enough.

357
00:26:28,905 --> 00:26:30,889
I'm sorry, sir.

358
00:26:30,889 --> 00:26:33,389
No, you have nothing to apologize for.

359
00:26:33,389 --> 00:26:35,204
I was the one who sent you.

360
00:26:35,204 --> 00:26:37,725
If we weren't prepared enough, that's on me.

361
00:26:37,725 --> 00:26:39,321
No, it's not.

362
00:26:39,321 --> 00:26:42,569
I should've done more.

363
00:26:42,569 --> 00:26:44,237
I'm sorry, sir.

364
00:26:44,237 --> 00:26:47,737
<i>No. You've worked hard enough today.
Go home and get some rest.</i>

365
00:26:47,737 --> 00:26:50,085
Yes, Mr. Gong.

366
00:26:50,085 --> 00:26:52,204
See you tomorrow.

367
00:27:00,737 --> 00:27:04,204
Doesn't this mean it's all over?

368
00:27:06,737 --> 00:27:09,361
[Choi Joo Hee, Assistant Manager, Team 2]

369
00:27:09,361 --> 00:27:11,541
Oh, Joo Hee, did you find out?

370
00:27:11,541 --> 00:27:14,605
<i>Mr. Joo, it's Mantua.</i>

371
00:27:14,605 --> 00:27:16,470
- Mantua?
<i>- Yes.</i>

372
00:27:16,470 --> 00:27:20,821
<i>They seem to think CGM's
ultimate target is China through Korea.</i>

373
00:27:20,821 --> 00:27:22,913
Hongsung plans
to sign an exclusive deal with Mantua

374
00:27:22,913 --> 00:27:25,781
and enter China before CGM.

375
00:27:25,781 --> 00:27:27,717
So Hongsung is targeting China?

376
00:27:27,717 --> 00:27:31,617
<i>Yes, Mantua's Head of Merchandising
came to the office this morning.</i>

377
00:27:31,617 --> 00:27:33,317
<i>I'm sure.</i>

378
00:27:47,137 --> 00:27:48,137
Hello.

379
00:27:48,137 --> 00:27:49,797
<i>Mr. Sponza.</i>

380
00:27:49,797 --> 00:27:51,165
<i>Mr. Jung.</i>

381
00:27:51,165 --> 00:27:53,337
<i>I was expecting your call.</i>

382
00:27:53,337 --> 00:27:56,573
I heard your CMO is in Korea.

383
00:27:56,573 --> 00:27:58,509
Are you worried
that I might take their offer?

384
00:27:58,509 --> 00:27:59,717
<i>You know,</i>

385
00:27:59,717 --> 00:28:01,921
this is important to me.

386
00:28:01,921 --> 00:28:03,569
You don't need to worry.

387
00:28:03,569 --> 00:28:06,270
Not necessary to stand against CGM.

388
00:28:08,109 --> 00:28:10,701
Have you made up your mind?

389
00:28:10,701 --> 00:28:13,970
Thieves fight if they want the same thing.

390
00:28:14,909 --> 00:28:19,701
Okay, we'll consider Mantua
having no interest in China.

391
00:28:19,701 --> 00:28:21,181
I'll see you soon.

392
00:28:21,181 --> 00:28:22,881
<i>Sure.</i>

393
00:28:48,573 --> 00:28:50,937
You seem pretty busy these days.

394
00:28:52,837 --> 00:28:55,825
Oh, a little... yes.

395
00:28:55,825 --> 00:28:57,301
You can tell?

396
00:28:57,301 --> 00:29:00,073
You notice things when you run a café.

397
00:29:00,073 --> 00:29:02,657
Whether someone's busy or free,

398
00:29:02,657 --> 00:29:06,437
whether they enjoy their work or hate it.
Things like that.

399
00:29:06,437 --> 00:29:08,689
You look busy.

400
00:29:08,689 --> 00:29:12,337
Don't you dislike seeing people
who look busy first thing in the morning?

401
00:29:12,337 --> 00:29:13,904
What are you talking about?

402
00:29:13,904 --> 00:29:16,904
That's why I open the café in the morning.

403
00:29:16,904 --> 00:29:20,253
People are more productive in the morning.

404
00:29:20,253 --> 00:29:22,033
"Productive."

405
00:29:22,033 --> 00:29:23,905
That's a nice way to put it.

406
00:29:23,905 --> 00:29:27,729
I thought things would slow down there,

407
00:29:27,729 --> 00:29:29,770
but you're even busier now.

408
00:29:30,981 --> 00:29:32,681
It's interesting.

409
00:29:33,389 --> 00:29:35,270
Hang in there today.

410
00:29:36,357 --> 00:29:38,057
Thanks.

411
00:29:59,237 --> 00:30:02,437
[Orenda Outlet, Paradis Mall Outlet]

412
00:30:02,437 --> 00:30:05,070
[Transfer Confirmation]

413
00:30:05,070 --> 00:30:06,704
[Shinhwa BKC, Hongsung International]

414
00:30:06,704 --> 00:30:09,037
[Completed]

415
00:30:09,037 --> 00:30:10,604
[Transfer Confirmation]

416
00:30:10,604 --> 00:30:12,670
[List of Penalty Payments
by Country and Brand]

417
00:30:12,670 --> 00:30:15,337
[Need to check
whether standard contracts are used]

418
00:30:16,904 --> 00:30:18,104
[Confirmation of Penalty Payment]

419
00:30:18,104 --> 00:30:20,237
[This confirmation is intended to
prevent any future legal disputes...]

420
00:30:20,237 --> 00:30:22,637
[Finance Team,
Cancellation penalty status uploaded]

421
00:30:22,637 --> 00:30:23,804
[List of Penalty Payments
by Country and Brand]

422
00:30:23,804 --> 00:30:25,537
[Download]

423
00:30:26,404 --> 00:30:27,837
[Brand Europe, Brand Asia]

424
00:30:27,837 --> 00:30:30,537
[Payment Status]

425
00:30:32,737 --> 00:30:36,137
[Paradis Mall Outlet, 5,600,000,000 won]

426
00:30:38,685 --> 00:30:41,233
Yeah, Paradis Mall's deposit didn't come in.

427
00:30:41,233 --> 00:30:43,273
Put some pressure on them.

428
00:30:43,273 --> 00:30:46,065
Mr. Yang, Paradis Mall
hasn't paid the penalty.

429
00:30:46,065 --> 00:30:47,525
I'll call them.

430
00:30:47,525 --> 00:30:48,573
Will that be okay?

431
00:30:48,573 --> 00:30:51,170
For me? Or for Paradis Mall?

432
00:30:52,270 --> 00:30:54,970
[Hongsung Punk]

433
00:30:54,970 --> 00:30:56,704
Darn it.

434
00:31:00,221 --> 00:31:02,437
- What's going...
<i>- We haven't received your payment yet.</i>

435
00:31:02,437 --> 00:31:03,701
- Our finance team...
<i>- Please hurry it up.</i>

436
00:31:03,701 --> 00:31:05,169
We are itching to sue.

437
00:31:05,169 --> 00:31:07,804
- If you want to sue...
- Call back after you pay.

438
00:31:11,465 --> 00:31:14,373
This little punk, seriously.

439
00:31:14,373 --> 00:31:16,204
What happened with the penalty?

440
00:31:16,204 --> 00:31:19,304
They said Finance would send it.

441
00:31:19,304 --> 00:31:22,789
Tell them to hurry up.
I don't want calls like this anymore.

442
00:31:22,789 --> 00:31:24,404
Yes, sir.

443
00:31:24,404 --> 00:31:27,337
Once we transfer the penalty
and fax it to CGM...

444
00:31:27,337 --> 00:31:30,104
Hurry, hurry, hurry!

445
00:31:36,117 --> 00:31:37,817
Ms. Joo.

446
00:31:40,970 --> 00:31:43,737
[Transfer Confirmation]

447
00:31:43,737 --> 00:31:46,470
[Transfer Confirmation]

448
00:31:49,437 --> 00:31:52,937
[Team Leader Joo Sun Ah]

449
00:31:52,937 --> 00:31:53,937
Yes?

450
00:31:53,937 --> 00:31:56,817
I've compiled the companies
that paid Hongsung's penalties.

451
00:31:56,817 --> 00:31:58,237
Good.

452
00:31:58,237 --> 00:31:59,404
Send them the new contracts.

453
00:31:59,404 --> 00:32:01,641
<i>Okay. Congratulations, Mr. Jung.</i>

454
00:32:01,641 --> 00:32:03,837
You're really going to
hit them hard, aren't you?

455
00:32:04,473 --> 00:32:07,037
This isn't something to celebrate.

456
00:32:07,037 --> 00:32:10,070
The roles of the powerful and the powerless
always change in this business.

457
00:32:13,541 --> 00:32:17,037
Place both hands and knees on the floor.

458
00:32:17,037 --> 00:32:21,837
Lift your back leg toward
the ceiling and slowly extend it.

459
00:32:21,837 --> 00:32:25,433
Slide your left arm along the floor
and reach it forward.

460
00:32:25,433 --> 00:32:27,493
And breathe.

461
00:32:27,493 --> 00:32:32,137
Now, from there, reach your left arm back
and grab your foot.

462
00:32:32,137 --> 00:32:36,537
Stretch through the front of your thigh
and look into the distance.

463
00:32:36,537 --> 00:32:38,070
Good.

464
00:32:38,070 --> 00:32:40,705
Now, press your arms firmly into the floor,

465
00:32:40,705 --> 00:32:42,937
and reach your fingertips toward the ceiling.

466
00:32:42,937 --> 00:32:44,670
That's it.

467
00:32:46,970 --> 00:32:48,101
[Secretary Choi]

468
00:32:48,101 --> 00:32:49,969
Good. Keep breathing.

469
00:32:49,969 --> 00:32:52,204
- Excuse me. I'm sorry.
- It's fine.

470
00:32:54,549 --> 00:32:56,249
Yeah? What is it?

471
00:32:57,669 --> 00:32:58,837
What?

472
00:32:58,837 --> 00:33:02,670
[Kim Soon Wook, Executive Director,
Belmore Department Store]

473
00:33:09,621 --> 00:33:12,321
<i>The subscriber you are calling
is not available. After the tone...</i>

474
00:33:12,321 --> 00:33:13,889
What? He's not answering?

475
00:33:13,889 --> 00:33:15,705
What do I do?

476
00:33:15,705 --> 00:33:19,204
I'll just make one important call.
Just a moment.

477
00:33:37,021 --> 00:33:38,021
Yes, Executive Director Kim.

478
00:33:38,021 --> 00:33:39,317
<i>Hello?</i>

479
00:33:39,317 --> 00:33:41,589
What do you think you're doing? Huh?

480
00:33:41,589 --> 00:33:43,004
<i>Oh, it's exactly as you saw.</i>

481
00:33:43,004 --> 00:33:46,485
We're lowering the commission
to 15% for luxury brands.

482
00:33:46,485 --> 00:33:48,693
Are you kidding me? Huh?

483
00:33:48,693 --> 00:33:51,977
Didn't you break the contract with Hongsung
because we'd cover the penalties?

484
00:33:51,977 --> 00:33:53,929
Turn the music off.

485
00:33:53,929 --> 00:33:56,237
You pull this
right after we paid the penalties?

486
00:33:56,237 --> 00:33:57,461
<i>Aren't you crossing the line here?</i>

487
00:33:57,461 --> 00:34:00,361
Are you doing business here,
or are you playing games?

488
00:34:00,361 --> 00:34:02,304
I said turn that music off!

489
00:34:05,033 --> 00:34:08,777
<i>Executive Director,
business is simple, as you know.</i>

490
00:34:08,777 --> 00:34:10,523
We made the offer because we knew it'd work.

491
00:34:10,523 --> 00:34:12,805
If you don't like it, you can refuse.

492
00:34:12,805 --> 00:34:16,985
If you don't agree to the new contract,
we won't cover the penalties.

493
00:34:16,985 --> 00:34:19,670
If you keep playing this way,

494
00:34:19,670 --> 00:34:21,004
it won't just be us.

495
00:34:21,004 --> 00:34:23,245
<i>The other department stores
won't stand for it either.</i>

496
00:34:23,245 --> 00:34:24,504
<i>Are you ready for the consequences?</i>

497
00:34:24,504 --> 00:34:27,189
We're not doing this
to every department store.

498
00:34:27,189 --> 00:34:30,829
We won't do this to stores
that reached a reasonable agreement.

499
00:34:30,829 --> 00:34:34,321
<i>We've already exceeded
our store acquisition target.</i>

500
00:34:34,321 --> 00:34:39,593
If you don't like these terms,
you can sign with Hongsung again.

501
00:34:39,593 --> 00:34:41,704
Mr. Jung!

502
00:34:41,704 --> 00:34:44,804
Don't raise your voice, Mr. Kim.

503
00:34:44,804 --> 00:34:49,270
You're just an executive director.
Why do you keep talking down to me?

504
00:34:50,481 --> 00:34:51,593
Mr. Kim,

505
00:34:51,593 --> 00:34:56,737
let's show each other some respect
and do business, shall we?

506
00:34:56,737 --> 00:34:59,537
Take some time to consider it
and get back to me.

507
00:34:59,537 --> 00:35:02,285
Oh, and take good care of yourself.

508
00:35:02,285 --> 00:35:04,809
<i>Executives always seem to
get sick after they retire.</i>

509
00:35:04,809 --> 00:35:08,261
Some even pass away sooner than expected.

510
00:35:08,261 --> 00:35:10,149
You!

511
00:35:10,149 --> 00:35:11,897
Hey... hello?

512
00:35:11,897 --> 00:35:13,065
Hey!

513
00:35:45,405 --> 00:35:47,970
What happened with the penalties?

514
00:35:49,869 --> 00:35:51,670
We've got all of them back.

515
00:35:51,670 --> 00:35:56,004
They didn't put up much of a fight,
probably thinking CGM would cover it.

516
00:35:57,770 --> 00:35:59,813
I feel like I'm getting indigestion.

517
00:35:59,813 --> 00:36:01,904
- Let's get started.
- Yes, ma'am.

518
00:36:12,004 --> 00:36:13,470
Yes, Reporter Park.

519
00:36:13,470 --> 00:36:15,773
You can publish it now.

520
00:36:15,773 --> 00:36:18,204
Yes, thank you.

521
00:36:23,389 --> 00:36:27,870
The highest rental fees are based
on customer traffic patterns.

522
00:36:31,237 --> 00:36:32,970
Hello.

523
00:36:33,857 --> 00:36:35,825
What?

524
00:36:35,825 --> 00:36:37,525
Okay.

525
00:36:41,737 --> 00:36:45,870
[Hongsung's Massive Counterattack,
Will CGM's Expansion into Korea Fail?]

526
00:36:51,070 --> 00:36:54,670
I just heard about it myself.
I'll look into it and get back to you.

527
00:36:54,670 --> 00:36:56,870
Well... Mr. Jung.

528
00:36:56,870 --> 00:36:59,004
L-Look at this...

529
00:37:01,037 --> 00:37:02,204
[CGM's Attempt to Crush Korean Firms,
Who's actually getting crushed?]

530
00:37:02,204 --> 00:37:04,404
What's this?

531
00:37:04,404 --> 00:37:08,004
[Department Stores' Complicated Calculations,
Hongsung or CGM?]

532
00:37:15,404 --> 00:37:16,970
Mr. Jung!

533
00:37:16,970 --> 00:37:18,270
What's going on?

534
00:37:18,270 --> 00:37:21,669
I thought Mantua wasn't going to
partner with Hongsung.

535
00:37:21,669 --> 00:37:25,301
Hongsung just took over
all storage units in Shenzhen.

536
00:37:25,301 --> 00:37:27,937
80% of Mantua's brands clash with ours.

537
00:37:27,937 --> 00:37:31,970
If they enter China first, everything
we've been working toward is useless.

538
00:37:31,970 --> 00:37:33,870
I made it clear so many times

539
00:37:33,870 --> 00:37:37,537
that we don't need to
enter the Korean market this way.

540
00:37:37,537 --> 00:37:39,870
Are you listening to me?

541
00:37:51,137 --> 00:37:55,670
[Hongsung Partners with Mantua
to Enter the Chinese Market]

542
00:37:56,465 --> 00:37:59,305
Oh, why? I swear I'll keep it to myself.

543
00:37:59,305 --> 00:38:00,381
Please.

544
00:38:00,381 --> 00:38:03,504
I'm just really worried.

545
00:38:11,817 --> 00:38:13,370
The coffee's hot, right?

546
00:38:13,370 --> 00:38:16,404
- Pardon?
- Put it down before you burn yourself.

547
00:38:17,113 --> 00:38:18,837
Okay.

548
00:38:22,689 --> 00:38:23,937
Huh?

549
00:38:23,937 --> 00:38:26,205
[Voice Recording]

550
00:38:26,205 --> 00:38:30,004
Are you going to unlock it,
or should I call the Internal Audit?

551
00:38:32,970 --> 00:38:34,704
Unlock it.

552
00:38:43,493 --> 00:38:45,104
[Team Leader Joo, Sales Team 3]
<i>How about staying here</i>

553
00:38:45,104 --> 00:38:48,070
and being our eyes and ears?

554
00:38:50,470 --> 00:38:51,657
Ms. Joo,

555
00:38:51,657 --> 00:38:55,204
I'll switch companies if you tell me to.

556
00:38:55,204 --> 00:38:58,004
But I can't do that.

557
00:39:02,097 --> 00:39:03,485
Actually, never mind.

558
00:39:03,485 --> 00:39:05,513
I won't even leave the company.

559
00:39:05,513 --> 00:39:07,213
Get lost.

560
00:39:10,737 --> 00:39:14,104
<i>No, you've had a long day.
Go home and get some rest.</i>

561
00:39:14,104 --> 00:39:16,604
Yes, Mr. Gong.

562
00:39:17,497 --> 00:39:19,304
See you tomorrow.

563
00:39:19,304 --> 00:39:21,337
[Lee Ji Hye, Associate, Team 5]

564
00:39:28,237 --> 00:39:31,237
[Martina]

565
00:39:35,537 --> 00:39:37,289
Yes, Director, this is Gong Eun Tae.

566
00:39:37,289 --> 00:39:40,670
I'll be in the office tomorrow.
Please prepare the contract.

567
00:39:42,270 --> 00:39:43,953
You're signing the contract?

568
00:39:43,953 --> 00:39:45,729
<i>Your employee was impressive.</i>

569
00:39:45,729 --> 00:39:48,304
<i>She has great taste in clothes and food.</i>

570
00:39:48,304 --> 00:39:50,665
<i>Not that taste is what matters most.</i>

571
00:39:50,665 --> 00:39:52,470
There was just one thing.

572
00:39:52,470 --> 00:39:56,477
I wanted to see if she could make
a bad thing sound good.

573
00:39:56,477 --> 00:39:59,937
Tomorrow, have them send someone else.

574
00:40:02,897 --> 00:40:07,370
While we can't know Mantua's exact figures,

575
00:40:07,370 --> 00:40:09,470
we estimate Mantua

576
00:40:09,470 --> 00:40:13,189
would lose 12% of its sales
if CGM enters China.

577
00:40:13,189 --> 00:40:16,789
We estimate East Asian retailers
account for about that much.

578
00:40:16,789 --> 00:40:22,537
Mr. Gong believe we could capture over 5%
of the imported apparel market.

579
00:40:22,537 --> 00:40:26,573
I'll have the requested materials
sent to your hotel within 30 minutes.

580
00:40:26,573 --> 00:40:30,804
And I'll arrange for someone else
to come tomorrow.

581
00:40:30,804 --> 00:40:32,937
Will someone else

582
00:40:32,937 --> 00:40:35,317
be better than you?

583
00:40:35,317 --> 00:40:38,217
To be honest,

584
00:40:38,217 --> 00:40:43,004
even if our team leader shows up,
I don't think it'll make much difference.

585
00:40:44,337 --> 00:40:46,904
Mr. Gong said it himself.

586
00:40:46,904 --> 00:40:52,137
You can't do business with someone
who thinks they have you by the throat.

587
00:40:53,557 --> 00:40:55,533
We need Mantua.

588
00:40:55,533 --> 00:40:57,345
We're desperate.

589
00:40:57,345 --> 00:41:01,129
And I'm sure Mantua needs us too.

590
00:41:01,129 --> 00:41:04,865
So please show us the respect
we need to work together.

591
00:41:04,865 --> 00:41:07,437
Just as we show courtesy to you.

592
00:41:09,404 --> 00:41:11,437
I'll be going now.

593
00:41:24,965 --> 00:41:26,370
<i>The easiest thing in the world</i>

594
00:41:26,370 --> 00:41:30,185
<i>is to say good things nicely
and bad things harshly.</i>

595
00:41:30,185 --> 00:41:33,470
It's much harder
to make a bad thing sound good.

596
00:41:33,470 --> 00:41:36,970
But your staff member
managed to do just that.

597
00:41:36,970 --> 00:41:39,537
<i>I think we'll work well together.</i>

598
00:41:39,537 --> 00:41:40,537
Then

599
00:41:40,537 --> 00:41:43,137
<i>are you heading to China with us?</i>

600
00:41:44,470 --> 00:41:46,337
Let's talk about it tomorrow.

601
00:41:53,333 --> 00:41:54,641
Ms. Jang.

602
00:41:54,641 --> 00:41:56,037
Yes.

603
00:41:56,037 --> 00:41:58,437
Please reserve the warehouse in Shenzhen.

604
00:42:02,070 --> 00:42:03,337
Mantua?

605
00:42:03,337 --> 00:42:07,701
<i>They seem to think CGM's
ultimate target is China through Korea.</i>

606
00:42:07,701 --> 00:42:11,437
Mantua's Head of Merchandising
came to the office this morning.

607
00:42:11,437 --> 00:42:13,170
I'm sure.

608
00:42:18,833 --> 00:42:19,970
<i>Mr. Gong,</i>

609
00:42:19,970 --> 00:42:22,104
<i>I heard you decided to sign the contract.</i>

610
00:42:22,104 --> 00:42:24,170
Yes, I truly appreciate it.

611
00:42:24,170 --> 00:42:25,904
It wasn't my decision.

612
00:42:25,904 --> 00:42:27,704
Martina made this decision.

613
00:42:27,704 --> 00:42:31,237
<i>And the reason was
your employee is outstanding.</i>

614
00:42:31,237 --> 00:42:34,204
It was your decision in the end.

615
00:42:34,204 --> 00:42:37,137
Is there anything more I can do for you?

616
00:42:37,137 --> 00:42:40,093
You may receive a call from Jung Sun Hyuk.

617
00:42:40,093 --> 00:42:43,649
And should I just tell them
we're not going to sign with Hongsung?

618
00:42:43,649 --> 00:42:46,070
<i>I'll leave it in your hand, Mr. Sponza.</i>

619
00:42:46,070 --> 00:42:48,245
They won't change anything in the end.

620
00:42:48,245 --> 00:42:50,305
<i>I'll handle it myself.</i>

621
00:42:50,305 --> 00:42:53,004
Turns out the guy who came in
late at night work

622
00:42:53,004 --> 00:42:55,473
was actually here to steal from me.

623
00:42:55,473 --> 00:42:59,437
I can't just let him walk away like that,
can I?

624
00:43:00,229 --> 00:43:03,237
Looks like we need to put on a show.

625
00:43:03,237 --> 00:43:05,961
There is a reason why Martina
is so good at acting.

626
00:43:05,961 --> 00:43:07,929
She learned from me.

627
00:43:07,929 --> 00:43:09,804
She's just Korean.

628
00:43:27,404 --> 00:43:29,737
[Yoon Seong Shik, Department Head,
Armonia Department Store]

629
00:43:29,737 --> 00:43:31,737
[Baek Mi Ha, Manager, Luceine]

630
00:43:31,737 --> 00:43:33,670
[Kang In Ja, Team Leader, Lorvenzo]

631
00:43:33,670 --> 00:43:36,270
[Yang Ji Sun, Manager, Oufic]

632
00:43:41,601 --> 00:43:44,070
I like moments like this.

633
00:43:45,477 --> 00:43:47,404
Moments that make you

634
00:43:48,349 --> 00:43:51,037
reinterpret the past.

635
00:43:58,821 --> 00:44:00,709
No matter how hard things get,

636
00:44:00,709 --> 00:44:04,404
once you pull through,
the past becomes a memory.

637
00:44:05,197 --> 00:44:09,970
If you don't, it becomes
a memory you'd rather forget.

638
00:44:11,925 --> 00:44:15,265
The past doesn't make the present.

639
00:44:15,265 --> 00:44:18,570
The present makes the past.

640
00:45:42,504 --> 00:45:45,204
Thank you for making time for me,
Executive Director.

641
00:45:47,204 --> 00:45:50,437
I was curious why you wanted to see me.

642
00:45:51,461 --> 00:45:54,685
You have a way of making people
wonder about all sorts of things.

643
00:45:54,685 --> 00:45:57,770
It's not something
I could say over the phone.

644
00:45:58,804 --> 00:46:00,570
What is it?

645
00:46:03,173 --> 00:46:05,321
Sir,

646
00:46:05,321 --> 00:46:08,070
are you planning to retire from Hongsung?

647
00:46:10,637 --> 00:46:12,601
What are you getting at?

648
00:46:12,601 --> 00:46:14,537
We'd like you

649
00:46:14,537 --> 00:46:17,070
to join CGM.

650
00:46:23,085 --> 00:46:24,085
In what capacity?

651
00:46:24,085 --> 00:46:27,604
Whatever position you desire,
executive director, senior advisor, anything.

652
00:46:27,604 --> 00:46:28,604
What are the terms?

653
00:46:28,604 --> 00:46:31,497
We're thinking around 500,000 dollars.

654
00:46:31,497 --> 00:46:33,197
What do you say?

655
00:46:40,149 --> 00:46:44,381
Actually, I think leaving
was the right move for you.

656
00:46:44,381 --> 00:46:46,565
That's just how companies work.

657
00:46:46,565 --> 00:46:49,233
Sometimes they let good people slip away.

658
00:46:49,233 --> 00:46:53,269
Goodness, I guess it just
wasn't the right fit.

659
00:46:53,269 --> 00:46:54,269
Oh, come on.

660
00:46:54,269 --> 00:46:58,209
Anyway, it's nice to see
someone from Hongsung doing well.

661
00:46:58,209 --> 00:47:00,437
I just have to work harder.

662
00:47:01,145 --> 00:47:02,870
By the way,

663
00:47:03,570 --> 00:47:06,837
what are your plans for CGM?

664
00:47:06,837 --> 00:47:09,337
No matter how I look at it,

665
00:47:09,337 --> 00:47:12,125
you can't make it work in Korea
with these margins.

666
00:47:12,125 --> 00:47:15,189
You think the margins are too low?

667
00:47:15,189 --> 00:47:18,537
You want to secure the market first?

668
00:47:18,537 --> 00:47:19,537
Yes.

669
00:47:19,537 --> 00:47:23,861
I want to establish ourselves early,
even if we have to push a little.

670
00:47:23,861 --> 00:47:27,425
Come on, there must be more to it, huh?

671
00:47:27,425 --> 00:47:30,804
We're going to be working together now.
Can't you tell me?

672
00:47:32,285 --> 00:47:33,349
Sir.

673
00:47:35,637 --> 00:47:38,137
Are you really joining CGM?

674
00:47:39,489 --> 00:47:41,793
Well, I told you I am.

675
00:47:41,793 --> 00:47:43,493
Sir.

676
00:47:46,641 --> 00:47:47,704
Was it that obvious?

677
00:47:47,704 --> 00:47:48,704
Very.

678
00:47:48,704 --> 00:47:51,037
Jeez.

679
00:47:51,753 --> 00:47:54,537
Acting isn't as easy as it looks.

680
00:47:55,437 --> 00:47:58,113
Actors deserve every penny they make.

681
00:47:58,113 --> 00:48:02,004
Alright, my treat. Let's just have a drink.

682
00:48:11,737 --> 00:48:13,425
Then,

683
00:48:13,425 --> 00:48:17,904
assuming you're not coming,
let me ask you one thing.

684
00:48:19,370 --> 00:48:21,837
Why do you want to stay with Hongsung?

685
00:48:23,101 --> 00:48:25,641
You had it wrong from the start.

686
00:48:25,641 --> 00:48:27,341
What did I get wrong?

687
00:48:28,589 --> 00:48:31,470
I've been with Hongsung for 30 years.

688
00:48:31,470 --> 00:48:35,077
I've been with the CEO
since he started the company in that office

689
00:48:35,077 --> 00:48:37,904
above the Gwanghui-dong supermarket.

690
00:48:37,904 --> 00:48:42,237
Do you really think I'd leave now for money?

691
00:48:42,237 --> 00:48:46,570
Then what should I have offered?

692
00:48:47,270 --> 00:48:50,361
A bigger market, a grander vision,

693
00:48:50,361 --> 00:48:52,765
something like greater prestige.

694
00:48:52,765 --> 00:48:55,704
You should've approached me with those.

695
00:48:57,113 --> 00:48:59,570
Would you join, then?

696
00:49:02,137 --> 00:49:06,169
No. I still wouldn't.

697
00:49:06,169 --> 00:49:08,204
You're the same, aren't you?

698
00:49:09,329 --> 00:49:11,937
You don't work just for money.

699
00:49:14,737 --> 00:49:17,505
If you're that kind of person,

700
00:49:17,505 --> 00:49:21,370
why did you think I wasn't?

701
00:50:00,961 --> 00:50:03,670
So, you're saying you need to
keep secrets from me as well?

702
00:50:03,670 --> 00:50:05,389
If I were Jung Sun Hyuk,

703
00:50:05,389 --> 00:50:09,604
I figured you'd be the first person
I'd approach, sir.

704
00:50:10,233 --> 00:50:13,637
Anyway, Ms. Park is sharp as a tack.
